---
// Privacy Policy — PLACEHOLDER. See terms.astro for why this page exists.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalDraft from '../components/LegalDraft.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy · Aunt Mabel" noindex={true}>
  <LegalDraft heading="Privacy Policy" kicker="Legal">
    <p>
      This policy will describe how <strong>Cajun Relief Foundation, d/b/a
      Cajun Navy Ground Force</strong> handles information collected through
      the Aunt Mabel daily wellness-call service.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's being finalized with counsel now. When it's ready, this page will
      set out what we collect, why we collect it, how long we keep it, who it
      is shared with, and how to ask for it to be deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two things are worth stating up front, because they're the ones families
      ask about first:
    </p>
    <p class="emphasis">
      Daily calls are not recorded today. Preserving call recordings for
      families is a possible future feature, and it would require its own
      separate, explicit consent — it would never be switched on quietly for
      anyone already enrolled.
    </p>
    <p>
      The details a recipient shares on a call are used to check on their
      wellbeing and, if something sounds wrong, to alert the emergency contacts
      named during enrollment. A recipient's ZIP code is also used to know when
      a disaster has reached their area.
    </p>
  </LegalDraft>
</BaseLayout>
